          "create_time": 1750000001.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "My bare-metal k8s cluster has no cloud load balancer. I tried NodePort but the ports are ugly and I want real TLS on port 443."
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "n2": {
        "id": "n2",
        "parent": "n1",
        "children": ["n3"],
        "message": {
          "id": "n2",
          "author": { "role": "assistant" },
          "create_time": 1750000002.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Use MetalLB in L2 mode to hand out a real external IP, then put ingress-nginx in front of it and terminate TLS with cert-manager."
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "n3": {
        "id": "n3",
        "parent": "n2",
        "children": [],
        "message": {
          "id": "n3",
          "author": { "role": "user" },
          "create_time": 1750000003.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "That worked. I settled on MetalLB plus ingress-nginx and cert-manager with Let's Encrypt DNS-01, because HTTP-01 kept failing behind my router."
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  {
